export anchor TabloidStyle:
    number: 79
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Tabloid
    idea: The dashboard shouts like a tabloid front page, with a red masthead, a giant condensed splash for the overdue count, starburst stickers and every project in a tilted cut-out photo box.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fbfaf7, the page and photo frames
        ink: #0b0b0b, type, 3px borders, hard shadows and the nav strip
        mastheadRed: #c8102e, the masthead, the primary button, this week bars, the overdue fact box and Behind
        highlighter: #ffe100, fact boxes, starbursts, the current nav item and At risk, ink text only
        grey: #4a4a4a, captions under photo headlines
        halftone: #d9d6cf, the dot screen inside photo boxes
        cutoutGrey: #9a968e, silhouettes inside photo boxes, decoration only
        green: #0f6b33, the On track sticker
        focusBlue: #123e9c, the 4px focus outline
    type:
        Shouting type uses Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold,
        Franklin Gothic Heavy, condensed sans in caps. The splash is 132px
        at 0.86 line height, the masthead 76px italic set on a red block
        skewed 4 degrees, section bars 32px, photo headlines 26px, fact
        figures 64px and nav 18px. Body uses Arial, Helvetica Neue in bold
        at 22px for the deck and 15 to 16px for text.
    layout:
        A black nav strip runs across the top with caps links, Home on
        yellow, and Signed in Mara Okafor at the right. The masthead is a
        skewed red block with Brightwork in white italic and a small strap,
        casting a 6px ink shadow, beside the date in caps over a thick rule,
        a boxed FIND search, a red New project button and a yellow starburst
        reading 3 new. The splash sits between 6px rules, a yellow tilted
        kicker Morning, Mara, the headline 4 TASKS OVERDUE with the first
        words red, a bold deck with Billing migration highlighted, and a big
        rotated yellow starburst reading 73 done this week. Four yellow fact
        boxes tilt alternately with hard shadows, the overdue box red. The
        main area is The big six, a grid of tilted white photo boxes, each
        with a halftone picture of a simple drawn object such as a browser,
        phone, clipboard, card, book or envelope, a black percent flag in
        the corner, a caps headline, a meta line and a status sticker. Team
        gossip runs beside it with caps names and red time chips. The
        fortnight that was is a boxed bar chart with a red hard shadow,
        white bars last week, red bars this week and big numbers on top. At
        375px the photos stack in one column and the burst moves under the
        splash.
    spacing: An 8px unit, loud and packed. 16 to 22px between boxes and 6px rules between blocks.
    density: Medium. Few words, each one huge.
    corners: Square boxes. Only the On track sticker is a pill. Boxes tilt by 1 to 2 degrees.
    borders: 3px ink on boxes and fields, 4 to 6px ink rules above and below the splash.
    shadows: Hard offset ink shadows of 4 to 8px with no blur. The chart casts a red one.
    icons:
        Stickers with different shapes. A green disc with a tick on a white
        pill for On track, a yellow sign with a black triangle for At risk
        and a red jagged burst with a cross for Behind. Starbursts hold the
        big numbers.
    focus: A 4px focus blue outline offset 2px.
    tone: Exclaiming headlines, such as Morning, Mara, 4 tasks overdue, Shock as, The big six and Team gossip.
